This doesn't sound like the wizards I played. For one thing spell
skills are cheaper than weapon skills (1-1-2 instead of 1-2-3). The
only instances where I ever ran out of skill slots were early-midgame
wizards who trained several schools to Expert. A second thing is that
the robe bonus is insufficient to offset the body armor penalty (no
wizard would want ~30% failure rates) which means that spellcasting
wizards are already out of common armor. A third thing is that the
main wizard spell(tm) you will cast in combat is the wizard's special
which you can cast better than others, at 0% failure while wearing
both GoP and a small shield (and no robe).

As a wizard, I found robes only useful if I insist on wearing GoP and
have 0% (rather than 3%) at spells like 'cure sickness' at the same
time. This is already a debatable choice, since a strength of 18 is
quite sufficient.

